          {
            "point": "Standard mouthpieces and tubing"
          }
        ],
        "primary": {
          "eyebrow": "How it works",
          "title": "An embouchure made of a voice coil",
          "body": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "A trumpet player shapes the sound with air pressure and the vibration of the lips. Brass Core does the same in a sealed pressure chamber: a voice-coil motor, driven by your audio signal, modulates the air at the mouthpiece.",
              "spans": []
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The instrument is not a loudspeaker housing. The vibration excites the natural resonance of the brass itself, so the tone comes from the trumpet or trombone, with its own colour and projection.",
              "spans": []
            }
          ],
